    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74362" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύ̆-πτερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sharp-</i> or
				<i>swift-winged</i>: as Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ., ὁ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύσχοινος</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.52
			</span></i> ; but, <i>hawk,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Clem.Al.
				<u>Strom.</u>
				5.8.52.1
			</span></i> (in citation of <i><span class="en">
				<u>De.</u>
				14.13
			</span></i>) :—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύ̆-πτερον</span></b> , τό, =
			<i>falco,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὀξύπτερα</span>”
				<i>swift wings,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aesop.
					8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
